{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO no-fault eviction relocation assistance","requirement":"For no-fault terminations such as owner or relative occupancy, resident manager, demolition or withdrawal from rental use, government order to vacate, or conversion, the landlord must file a Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD first and pay relocation assistance.","key_value":"$11,000–$14,400 eligible; $23,150–$27,400 qualified (7/1/2026–6/30/2027)","coverage_conditions":"Units covered by the Rent Stabilization Ordinance; relocation is paid per unit, not per tenant.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"No-fault eviction of a covered unit; amount depends on the tenant's eligible, qualified or low income status and length of tenancy.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Replacing a resident manager with another resident manager; eviction required by hazardous conditions from a natural disaster not caused by landlord negligence; Mom and Pop properties with four or fewer units may pay reduced amounts.","penalty":"Failure to file the Landlord Declaration makes the eviction a violation of the RSO; non-payment of relocation assistance may be raised as an affirmative defense.","effective_date":"2026-07-01","valid_through":"2027-06-30","citation":"Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance (L.A.M.C. §151.00 et seq.)","quoted_span":"All tenant not- at-fault evictions require payment of relocation assistance and the filing of a Declaration of Intent to Evict form with the Los Angeles Housing Department (LAHD) before evicting tenants from units covered by the Rent Stabilization Ordinance (RSO) or the Just Cause Ordinance (JCO).","interaction":"RSO demolition evictions are treated as Ellis Act (Cal. Gov. Code 7060.4) evictions and must follow LAMC 151.22-151.28.","relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"JCO no-fault eviction relocation assistance","requirement":"For no-fault terminations of JCO-covered units the landlord must file a Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD and pay relocation assistance within 15 days of notice; a natural-person owner of a single-family dwelling pays one month's rent.","key_value":"$11,000–$14,400 eligible; $23,150–$27,400 qualified (7/1/2026–6/30/2027); 1 month's rent for a natural-person owner of a single-family dwelling","coverage_conditions":"Units covered by the Just Cause Ordinance; relocation is paid per unit.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"No-fault eviction of a covered unit; amount depends on the tenant's eligible, qualified or low income status and length of tenancy.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Replacing a resident manager with another resident manager; eviction required by hazardous conditions from a natural disaster not caused by landlord negligence; Mom and Pop properties with four or fewer units may pay reduced amounts.","penalty":"Failure to file the Landlord Declaration makes the eviction a violation of the JCO; non-payment of relocation assistance may be raised as an affirmative defense.","effective_date":"2026-07-01","valid_through":"2027-06-30","citation":"Los Angeles Just Cause Ordinance (L.A.M.C. §165.00 et seq.)","quoted_span":"All tenant not- at-fault evictions require payment of relocation assistance and the filing of a Declaration of Intent to Evict form with the Los Angeles Housing Department (LAHD) before evicting tenants from units covered by the Rent Stabilization Ordinance (RSO) or the Just Cause Ordinance (JCO).","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Resident Protections Ordinance relocation for demolition for new construction","requirement":"An owner demolishing a Protected Unit for new construction within 5 years of filing a Notice of Intent to Withdraw or Declaration of Intent to Evict must follow the RPO relocation options and pay the highest applicable State and City amount.","key_value":"demolition within 5 years of the LAHD filing; highest of State and City amounts","coverage_conditions":"Only Protected Units demolished for new construction; Protected Units include units subject to rent or price control within the past five years (all RSO units).","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"other","text":"Only Protected Units demolished for new construction; includes all RSO units and units under rent control in the past five years"}],"per_tenancy":"Demolition of the unit for new construction within 5 years of the LAHD filing","coverage_quotes":["The RPO only applies to Protected Units that will be demolished for the purpose of new construction."]},"exemptions":"Units that are not Protected Units or are not occupied by a lower income tenant are governed by the regular RSO or JCO relocation rules.","penalty":"Failure to comply may result in financial penalties starting at $250,000 per displaced unit and withholding of LAHD permit clearances.","effective_date":"2025-02-11","valid_through":null,"citation":"Los Angeles Resident Protections Ordinance (Ordinances #188481 and #188482)","quoted_span":"Failure to comply with the RPO may result in financial penalties starting at $250,000 per displaced unit and withholding of LAHD permit clearances.","interaction":"Owner must pay the highest of State (Housing Crisis Act) and City (RSO, JCO, RPO) relocation amounts.","relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Housing Crisis Act relocation for lower income households displaced by demolition","requirement":"For demolition of units where the owner will replace them with new construction, only lower income households (80% AMI or lower) receive relocation payments consistent with the benefits public entities must pay, and RSO or JCO amounts must be enhanced for them.","key_value":"80% AMI or lower","coverage_conditions":"Lower income households (80% AMI or lower) displaced by demolition for new construction.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Tenant is a lower income household (80% AMI or lower) displaced by demolition for new construction","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Cal. Gov. Code § 66300.6","quoted_span":"The City’s Resident Protections Ordinance (RPO) and the State’s Housing Crisis Act (HCA) require that ONLY lower income households (80%  AMI or lower) being displaced for demolition of their units where the owner will replace the units with new construction receive relocation payment consistent to the relocation benefits required to be paid by public entities under Chapter 16","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
